    "notes": "The dismantle warning is no longer on the card. It used to be three sentences standing permanently under every complex; the operator's ruling was that this is a mission control rather than a storybook, and a standing explanation of a button nobody has pressed is guidance. So the whole of it is the confirm step's own label, and this scene arms the press to show it. One complex rather than three, because the point is now the control rather than a comparison of three phrasings."
